Web Application Implementation Plan
This document outlines the strategy for building the GHCAA web presence, consisting of a public website and a secure member portal.

Architecture Overview
The system will follow a decoupled architecture:

Backend: ASP.NET Core API (Existing).
Public Web: A high-performance, SEO-friendly landing page and directory.
Member Portal: A secure, interactive Single Page Application (SPA).
User
Admin
Public Website / SEO
Member Portal SPA
ASP.NET Core API
Database
1. Public Website (public-web)
Features
Landing Page: Branding, vision, and mission.
News & Updates: Integrated with 
NewsService
.
Alumni Directory: Public search and basic profile views.
EC Members List: Dynamic view of current leadership.
Registration Flow: Multi-step application with document upload.
Aesthetics
Vibrant, professional palette (Deep Teal/Red/Gold).
Glassmorphism for cards.
Smooth scroll and reveal animations.
2. Member & Admin Portal (portal-app)
Features (Member)
Dashboard: Activity feed and announcements.
Digital ID & Certificate: Real-time generation and download.
Financials: View dues and submit payment proof.
Job Hub: Browse and post opportunities.
Chat: P2P messaging interface.
Features (Admin)
Member Approval: Workflow with document review.
Ledger Management: Record income and expenses.
Communication Center: Bulk emails and custom notifications.
Audit Logs: Comprehensive activity tracking.
3. Technology Stack
Framework: Angular (for enterprise-ready structure and robust tooling).
State Management: NgRx or Services with Signals.
Styling: SCSS with modern CSS variables (Flexbox/Grid).
API Client: Angular HttpClient with Interceptors for JWT and Global Loading.
Real-time: SignalR Client for Chat.
4. Mobile Considerations
Responsive Design: Mobile-first approach for all UI.
API Optimization: Standard JSON responses with proper HTTP status codes.
Token Persistence: Secure storage for JWT on mobile browsers/apps.
5. Verification Plan
Lighthouse Audit: Aiming for >90 on Performance and SEO.
Cross-Browser Testing: Chrome, Safari, Firefox, Edge.
Mobile Emulation: Thorough testing for touch targets and small screens.




Features Implementation Walkthrough
I have successfully completed the implementation of the Job Hub, Digital Identity, and System State Logic features, along with automated notifications and administrative statistics.

🚀 Key Features Implemented
9. API Mobile Readiness (NEW)
Framework Agnostic: Controllers refactored to use DTOs instead of Domain Models, preventing data leakage and ensuring robust API contracts.
DTOs Implemented: 
JobDto
, 
CreateJobDto
, 
PaymentHistoryDto
, 
MembershipDueDto
, 
NewsPostDto
.
Refactored Services: 
JobHubService
, 
FinancialService
, 
NewsService
 updated to map entities to DTOs.
Gallery Uploads: Added POST /api/gallery/upload-photo for mobile-friendly photo uploads.
Dynamic Fee Config: Admins can now configure membership fees by type and date via POST /api/financials/fees/config.
1. Job & Mentorship Hub
Job Posting: Members can post job opportunities via POST /api/jobs.
Public Browsing: Anonymous and registered users can browse job listings via GET /api/jobs.
Member-Specific Management: Members can manage their own postings.
2. Digital ID Card Generation
SVG-Based ID Cards: A dynamic SVG template generates high-quality digital ID cards.
Data URI Access: Members can retrieve their ID card as a Data URI for easy embedding or download.
Admin Access: Administrators can view any member's ID card.
3. System State Logic (Access Control)
Login Restrictions: 
Inactive
 and 
Archived
 members are strictly blocked from logging into the portal.
Search Privacy: 
Inactive
 and 
Archived
 members are hidden from all public directory searches.
Administrative Tools: Added endpoints for Reactivating members and Restoring archived records.
4. Public Alumni Directory (NEW)
Anonymous Search: Public users can now search for alumni via /api/networking/search (honoring privacy settings).
Detailed Public Profile: A dedicated endpoint /api/networking/member/{id} allows viewing a full public profile with photos.
Committee & Updates: Latest updates and EC lists are now public-accessible.
Advanced Community Features
Activity Feed: Real-time tracking of member logins and profile updates.
Bulk Photo Gallery: Admin-managed event galleries with bulk upload support.
P2P Chat: Direct messaging between alumni with unread message tracking.
Admin Audit Logging: Specialized tracking of administrative actions (Approval, Reactivation, Archival) with Actor tracking.
5. Admin Document Verification (NEW)
Attachment Review: Admins can fetch all member-uploaded paths (Photo, Certificate, Payment Proof) for approval via /api/admin/members/{id}/documents.
6. Membership Certificate (NEW)
Digital Certificates: Admins and members can generate a high-quality SVG Membership Certificate via 
GenerateCertificateDataUriAsync
.
7. Enhanced Communication (NEW)
Direct Custom Email: Admins can now send a one-off, non-templated email directly to any member by ID.
Bulk Sending: Already supported via Passing Year or Membership Type.
8. Admin Dashboard Statistics
Real-time Insights: Endpoint /api/admin/stats provides total member counts and financial balance.
🧪 Verification & Testing
122 Automated Tests: Covering authentication, networking, financials, and the new state logic.
Privacy Compliance: Strictly verified that Search/Profiles hide PII (Mobile/Email/Address) based on user preferences.
Test Suite Results
All core services have been verified with a total of 129 automated tests.

AuthService: Verified login restrictions for all membership states.
NetworkingService: Verified privacy compliance and visibility filtering for Inactive/Archived members.
FinancialService: Verified automated notification triggers, payment history, and dynamic fee configuration.
JobHubService: Verified CRUD operations and category-based filtering (DTO based).
